---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "@id": "https://shareitstudio.com/case-studies/pink-miracle#article",
  "headline": "Pink Miracle Case Study | Share It Studio",
  "description": "Turning Pink Miracle’s Loss into a $112K Win",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Share It Studio"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Share It Studio",
    // Optional: Add a logo if available
    // "logo": {
    //   "@type": "ImageObject",
    //   "url": "https://shareitstudio.com/logo.png"
    // }
  }
};

const breadcrumbListSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "@id": "https://shareitstudio.com/case-studies/pink-miracle#breadcrumb",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Home",
      "item": "https://shareitstudio.com/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Case Studies",
      "item": "https://shareitstudio.com/case-studies"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "Pink Miracle Case Study",
      "item": "https://shareitstudio.com/case-studies/pink-miracle"
    }
  ]
};

const combinedSchema = [articleSchema, breadcrumbListSchema];
---

<Layout 
  title="Pink Miracle Case Study | Share It Studio" 
  description="Turning Pink Miracle’s Loss into a $112K Win"
  schema={combinedSchema}
>
<article>
    <header>
      <h1>Case Study: Pink Miracle Amazon Listing & Video Ad Optimization</h1>
      <p>Turning Pink Miracle’s Loss into a $112K Win through data-driven content and sponsored ads optimization.</p>
    </header>

    <section id="client-background">
      <h2>Client Background</h2>
      <p><strong>Pink Miracle</strong> is a shoe cleaner brand with deep roots in California’s open-air markets. It has been selling a trusted product “since Jordan hit the scene.” From the start, it’s focused on crafting a shoe cleaner that truly resonates with sneakerheads and fashion enthusiasts alike, building a reputation for quality that stands the test of time.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="initial-challenge">
      <h2>Initial Challenge</h2>
      <p>Despite having a strong product and a well-established brand, Pink Miracle’s Amazon listing was lacking due to poor-quality content. Although they saw decent sales, their unoptimized listing led to lost revenue from low-quality images and videos and a weak overall presentation.</p>
      
      <p>Our connection with Pink Miracle came through networking, as a previous client referred them to us in October 2023 after they expressed dissatisfaction with their listing’s performance. The shared goal was clear: optimize their listing to increase revenue.</p>

      <section id="baseline-metrics">
        <h3>Baseline Metrics (At the Start of Engagement)</h3>
        <dl>
          <dt>Sessions</dt>
          <dd>4,966</dd>
          
          <dt>Units Ordered</dt>
          <dd>371</dd>
          
          <dt>Conversion Rate (CVR)</dt>
          <dd>24%</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section id="kpis">
        <h3>KPIs for the Video Ad</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>CVR:</strong> Conversion Rate</li>
          <li><strong>ROAS:</strong> Return on Ad Spend</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </section>

    <section id="our-approach">
      <h2>Our Approach</h2>
      <p>Our primary goal was to create data-driven content, including images, A+ Content, and sponsored ad videos. We aimed to test everything we produced and optimize the content based on results.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="implementation">
      <h2>Implementation</h2>
      <p>After analyzing the product’s demographics, keywords, and unique selling points (USPs), we created the first round of content: Images, Videos (Listing and Keyword-targeted Sponsored Ads), A+ Content, and Brand Story.</p>
      
      <p>Once the initial content round was created, we tested it across different platforms (PickFu and Intellivy). After this first round of testing, we optimized the content based on the results and repeated this process for the main images, secondary images, and image stack.</p>
      
      <p>For the video ad, we analyzed PPC data and campaigns and, based on that, created three groups of <em>[Pending Information]</em>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="results">
      <h2>Results</h2>
      <p><em>[Pending Information]</em></p>
    </section>

    <section id="key-takeaways">
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <p><em>[Pending Information]</em></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>